      "page_number": 1,
      "content": "Neural Layout Analysis for Voice Narration\nSpeech narration in digital reading systems requires extracting main body content while cleanly skipping tabular\ndata, captions, and running page headers.\nBenchmark Evaluation\nWe evaluate deep parsing models across structured academic articles and reports.\nArchitecture Precision Recall F1 Score\nBaseline Parser 82.4% 79.1% 80.7%\nDocling Hybrid 96.8% 95.4% 96.1%\nTable 1: Quantitative evaluation comparing baseline parser with Docling hybrid layout analysis.\nThe experimental results demonstrate that neural layout analysis prevents unnatural TTS reading of table cells\nand captions.\nPage 1 of 3 - Meta DeepRead Technical Report",
